## 3. Accessibility notes

### Toggle semantics and keyboard behaviour

- **Markup:** native `<input type="radio">` elements inside a `<fieldset>` with a visually hidden legend, "Billing period". The choice is mutually exclusive, so a radio group is the correct semantic. Don't use `aria-pressed` buttons or `role="tablist"`: tabs imply panels, and these are not panels.
- **Keyboard:** this is all native, so no custom key handling is needed.
  - Tab lands on the checked option (Annual by default).
  - Arrow keys move the selection and select at the same time, wrapping around.
  - Tab leaves the group.
- **Announcement:** "Billing period, group. Annual, Save 20%, radio button, checked, 2 of 2." The badge text becomes part of the label, which is the intent.
- **Focus:** the focus ring is drawn on the label through `:focus-visible`.
- **Forced colours:** in Windows High Contrast, the selected segment gets `Highlight`, because background fills are otherwise stripped.

### What screen readers announce when prices change

- A single polite `role="status"` region announces "Showing annual prices, billed yearly." (or the monthly equivalent).
- The prices themselves are **not** live regions. Six simultaneous updates would be noisy, and users hear the new values when they navigate the cards.
- The region is empty on page load, so nothing is announced initially.
- Prices read as "$15 per month". The visible "/mo" is `aria-hidden` and replaced with screen-reader-only text.
- **CTAs:**
  - Accessible names include the plan, for example "Start 14-day trial, Pro plan". The visible text comes first, which satisfies WCAG 2.5.3 (Label in Name).
  - While loading, the button uses `aria-disabled="true"` rather than `disabled`, so focus isn't dropped. Repeated clicks are ignored.
  - The status region announces "Starting your Pro plan…".

### Contrast (WCAG 2.2 AA)

| Pair | Ratio | Result |
|---|---|---|
| White on `--primary-600` (selected toggle, CTA, label) | 4.55:1 | Pass, with a thin margin. Never lighten primary-600 for text backgrounds. |
| White on `--primary-700` (hover) | 6.4:1 | Pass |
| `--gray-600` on white (unselected toggle) | 7.6:1 | Pass |
| `--gray-500` on white (suffix, billed line) | 4.8:1 | Pass |
| `--green-700` on `--green-50` (badge, 12px) | 5.3:1 | Pass |
| White on `--gray-500` (loading CTA) | 4.8:1 | Pass. Disabled controls are exempt, but it stays legible anyway. |
| Focus ring / check icon (`--primary-600`) vs white | 4.55:1 | Pass (non-text contrast needs 3:1) |
| `--gray-200` borders vs white | 1.24:1 | Decorative only. The toggle's selected state is carried by its 4.55:1 fill. |

